{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"code\": \"    def enqueue(self, message: Dict[str, Any]) -> bool:\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Attempt to add *message* to the dead-letter queue.\\n\\n        Returns ``True`` when the message is accepted, ``False`` when\\n        the queue is already at capacity.\\n\\n        BUG_63: the capacity guard now uses ``>=`` so the queue never\\n        exceeds ``max_size``.  It also fires the required capacity-\\n        warning alert once utilization reaches 80 %.\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        if len(self.queue) >= self.max_size:\\n            return False\\n\\n        self.queue.append(message)\\n\\n        utilization = self.utilization_pct\\n        if utilization >= 80.0:\\n            import orgops.alerts\\n            orgops.alerts.notify(\\n                \\\"dlq.capacity.warning\\\", {\\\"utilization_pct\\\": utilization}\\n            )\\n\\n        return True\\n\", \"comments\": \"Fix enqueue to reject at max_size and emit the dlq.capacity.warning alert once utilization hits 80%.\"}"}}
